alwaysApply: true
---

Read `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `docs/DOCUMENTATION_GOVERNANCE.md` before work.
The running system and source evidence outrank prose. Normative law lives in
`docs/specs/`; active work/status lives only in GitHub; `.scratchpad/` and
`docs/archive/` are historical and never select work.

Standing operational constraints:

- Work only inside the scope explicitly authorized by the current task.
- Execute known mechanical steps inside that scope; never demand a ceremonial trigger.
- Use isolated worktrees and explicit path staging. Never checkout, switch, restore,
  stash, hard-reset, or clean shared work.
- One ingest at a time. Never reset/drop the database without explicit authorization.
- Never start the live PostgreSQL cluster with `pg_ctl` or create hidden elevation.
- Never edit an executing `.cmd`; invoke Windows scripts through `cmd /c`.
- After engine rebuilds, rebuild/install extensions and verify the installed surface.
- Keep communication technical: no human relationship, therapeutic, or crisis framing.

Scoped implementation rules live in `.github/instructions/`; do not duplicate their
architecture or status here.
